{"chunks": [{"id": "9d458429eee9c627f1112f8eb994573514c1891038c0fde29e1d2c906358b105", "text": "Sample Company \u2013 HR Policies Short reference document for HR RAG / grounded Q&A; testing 1. Annual Leave Policy Full-time employees receive 20 days of paid annual leave per calendar year. Leave should normally be requested at least 5 working days in advance through the HR system. Managers may approve exceptions for urgent circumstances. 2. Sick Leave Policy Employees receive up to 10 paid sick days per calendar year. For an absence of more than 2 consecutive working days, the employee may be asked to provide appropriate medical documentation. 3. Work From Home Policy Eligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week with manager approval. Employees must remain reachable during their normal working hours and protect confidential company information while working remotely. 4. Travel & Expense Policy Business travel must be approved before booking. Employees should", "source": "sample_hr_policies.pdf", "page": 1}, {"id": "e8fcf52ea793934a613654d4c1d1d491f9366a30419fdcaee4011df6f0939cab", "text": "Work From Home Policy Eligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week with manager approval. Employees must remain reachable during their normal working hours and protect confidential company information while working remotely. 4. Travel & Expense Policy Business travel must be approved before booking. Employees should submit expense claims within 15 calendar days after returning from travel. Receipts are required for individual expenses above \u25a01,000. 5. Parental Leave Policy Eligible employees may receive parental leave according to applicable company policy and local law. Employees should contact HR as early as reasonably possible to plan leave and required documentation. 6. Code of Conduct Employees are expected to act professionally, avoid conflicts of interest, protect company information, and treat colleagues respectfully. Concerns about misconduct may be reported to HR or the designated ethics channel. 7. Performance Review Policy", "source": "sample_hr_policies.pdf", "page": 1}, {"id": "f703804491f7c7bafebd18c04c526da44ca3ef35a244913da7e38300a3d43b91", "text": "HR as early as reasonably possible to plan leave and required documentation. 6. Code of Conduct Employees are expected to act professionally, avoid conflicts of interest, protect company information, and treat colleagues respectfully. Concerns about misconduct may be reported to HR or the designated ethics channel. 7. Performance Review Policy Employees participate in a formal performance review at least once each year. Reviews consider role responsibilities, objectives, collaboration, and demonstrated performance. Quick Policy Facts Policy Key rule Annual leave 20 paid days/year Sick leave Up to 10 paid days/year Work from home Up to 2 days/week if eligible Expense claims Within 15 calendar days Receipt threshold Above \u25a01,000 Performance review At least annually Note: This is fictional sample content created for RAG testing and should not be treated as actual company policy.", "source": "sample_hr_policies.pdf", "page": 1}], "embeddings": [[0.05380137637257576, 0.06532596051692963, 0.040759727358818054, 0.011229352094233036, 0.081230528652668, 0.046544697135686874, 0.03960959240794182, -0.037893690168857574, -0.06234247609972954, -0.004714074078947306, 0.028996501117944717, -0.0067395661026239395, -0.045897673815488815, 0.019022639840841293, 0.06390716135501862, 0.005148905795067549, 0.0048789288848638535, -0.05446392670273781, -0.028898563235998154, -0.006064121145755053, 0.01535199023783207, -0.027568303048610687, -0.05749497190117836, 0.0011466756695881486, -0.03434505686163902, -0.00984975229948759, 0.03405848145484924, 0.028609951958060265, 0.019728517159819603, 0.0779908075928688, -0.024682244285941124, -0.028803816065192223, -0.0248273778706789, -0.04052063077688217, 0.018825838342308998, 7.462281246262137e-06, -0.019782917574048042, 